## 2. User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Role Mapping**: The backend has roles `DRIVER`, `FIELD_AGENT`, `MANAGER`, `OPS_EXECUTIVE`, `ACCOUNTS`, `OWNER`, `SUPER_ADMIN`. The app currently handles `DRIVER` and `FIELD_AGENT`. We need to confirm: should `MANAGER` and `OPS_EXECUTIVE` share the same app tab layout? And should `OWNER` have a separate, simplified read-only dashboard vs a full operational one?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Login Entry Point**: Currently one `LoginScreen` handles both roles via OTP. For Owner, do you want a **separate login screen selector** (choose role: Driver / Manager / Owner) before the OTP, or should the app detect role automatically after OTP verification (which is what the current backend already returns)?

> [!WARNING]
> **New Dependencies**: The plan requires adding `react-native-maps` (or `expo-maps` once stable), `react-native-chart-kit` or `victory-native` for the owner finance dashboard charts, and `expo-document-picker` for CN bilty upload. All must be tested against Expo SDK 54 compatibility before implementation.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Backend Driver ERP Access**: Drivers need to see their active trip, advance, and CN status. The backend currently exposes trips via `/api/erp/trips` but the authorize middleware only allows `['OWNER', 'MANAGER', 'OPS_EXECUTIVE', 'ACCOUNTS', 'SUPER_ADMIN']`. A new **driver-scoped trip view** endpoint (or loosening the authorize guard for read-only `DRIVER` access to their own trip) is required. This is a **backend change** that needs to be planned alongside the app.

> [!CAUTION]
> **POD via DRIVER_APP**: The POD model already has `receivedVia: 'DRIVER_APP'` as a valid enum value — the backend is ready for driver-initiated POD submission. But the POD route's authorize list needs to include `DRIVER`. Confirm this is intended before implementing.

